From 5e1a01eaa7610c9914dd4779a346190e5824f10d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:18:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(chamfer): no-pick 2D Chamfer leaves the model's sharp
 edges alone

A 2D Chamfer with no picks on a model that carries a modelled chamfer
at the top plane now rides only the bevelled edges. A sharp edge beside
them (a pocket rim the model leaves sharp) is not cut. A bevelled edge
whose enclosing edge is sharp refuses by name and asks for picks. A model
with no bevel at all still breaks every top edge (#303).

The program sim gives a no-pick chamfer on such a model no edge-break
credit (camcraft_sim::stock_sim::models_a_bevel), so a cut into a sharp
edge or a bevel wider than the modelled one is a gouge, also for a ride
cached by an older build.

Fixes #2596

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
